@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Bundled offline speech recognition
+
+This custom third-party debug build uses NVIDIA Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2,
+quantized to int8 and converted to ONNX by k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx. It is an
+English speech recognizer. Speech-to-text runs on the Android device, with
+no network inference, runtime model download, or saved microphone audio.
+The existing Sherpa-ONNX 2.0.1 arm64 AAR is reused.
+
+The English variant was selected after a four-phrase synthetic comparison
+on the Mac, where it retained ThinkStation P900 and Dell Precision more
+accurately than the v3 candidate. This is not a measurement of a user's voice
+or S24 performance. Real handset accuracy, latency, memory, and acoustic
+interruption tests remain required. Names can still be mistranscribed.
+
+## Sources and reproduction
+
+- Original weights: https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
+- Model license: CC BY 4.0; conversion/quantization is the upstream modification.
+- ONNX archive: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/asr-models/sherpa-onnx-nemo-parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-int8.tar.bz2
+- Archive SHA256: 6fc4426b54aa549a0019b8a75b8dea59164e71790a37ac56a045ad57f915f714
+- Silero VAD: https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx/releases/download/asr-models/silero_vad.onnx
+- Silero source and MIT license: https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
+
+Extract only encoder.int8.onnx, decoder.int8.onnx, joiner.int8.onnx and
+tokens.txt into parakeet-v2/. Place silero_vad.onnx beside that directory.
+Attributions and full license texts appear in the existing Licenses screen.
+
+## Behavior
+
+- Android 13+ arm64 custom build selects the private, explicit-component
+  ParakeetRecognitionService for conversation, PTT, dictation, and barge-in.
+- Other build variants retain Android's strictly on-device recognizer.
+- Silero VAD ends normal turns after 1.2 seconds of silence; the buffered
+  decoder supplies provisional partials, then a complete final result.
+- Supplied PCM pipes retain segmented sessions across ignored echo or speech.
+- Audio stays in bounded memory. A 90-second utterance limit reports an error
+  rather than submitting a truncated instruction. Cancellation clears buffers.
+- Qwen, Alba, wake detection, pairing, tools and permissions are unchanged.
+
+## Model file checksums
+
+- `silero_vad.onnx` (643854 bytes): `9e2449e1087496d8d4caba907f23e0bd3f78d91fa552479bb9c23ac09cbb1fd6`
+- `parakeet-v2/tokens.txt` (9384 bytes): `ec182b70dd42113aff6c5372c75cac58c952443eb22322f57bbd7f53977d497d`
+- `parakeet-v2/joiner.int8.onnx` (1739080 bytes): `77a29f3e5ac7d37074e0af465391b80f314015d5b97f0f90c6c7767f1d56f428`
+- `parakeet-v2/decoder.int8.onnx` (7257753 bytes): `4d097bae3bac5c96018d5293ba39f1b657296102b142affda40378f38b020f41`
+- `parakeet-v2/encoder.int8.onnx` (652282309 bytes): `92a10bd9c23936ea0566c29f963bc57c2a5df4261b6a8921c39abea66557ca8b`
